# Developer-local Claude Code config for working IN this repo. These hold
# per-machine paths and personal permission allowlists — never commit them.
# settings.local.json is Claude Code's own local-override convention;
# settings.json is added here explicitly because Claude Code does NOT ignore it
# by default (it treats it as a shared project file), and in this repo it must
# not be committed — see AGENTS.md.
/.claude/settings.json
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Per-instance state dirs are runtime — keep only the README placeholder.
# Default hooks/settings come from claude-sandbox-shared/, not from any
# instance dir.
claude-sandbox-persistent-state-*/*
!claude-sandbox-persistent-state-*/README.md

# Shared dir is also runtime, but track the default hooks scripts so a fresh
# clone has working hooks on first launch.
claude-sandbox-shared/*
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/
claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/*
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/hooks/
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/hooks/**
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/CLAUDE.md
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/settings.json
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/.caveman-active
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/PLUGIN_PINS.md
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/skills/
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/skills/**
# Vendor the caveman plugin source so a fresh clone has it without
# network round-trips to JuliusBrussee/caveman at first session. Pinned
# at v2.7.0 (commit 8b0c1d36...) — bump by replacing the tree in place
# and updating PLUGIN_PINS.md. The plugins/cache/ dir stays gitignored;
# claude-code rebuilds it from the vendored marketplaces tree on first
# session.
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/caveman/
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/caveman/**
# Vendor ponytail same way — pinned at v4.9.0 (commit 0a4dd63a...).
# See PLUGIN_PINS.md for bump procedure.
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/ponytail/
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/ponytail/**


workspace/*
!workspace/README.md
set_working_dir.sh

# Ignore the contents of the context folder:
context_reference/*
!context_reference/README.md

SAVED_SNAPSHOTS

# Per-instance env files are user-specific. Only the template is tracked.
env.sh
env.*.sh
!env.example.sh
!env.podman.example.sh
!env.gcp.example.sh

# Vertex-mode activation script holds a real GCP project id. Only the
# placeholder template is tracked.
SET_VERTEX_MODE.sh
!SET_VERTEX_MODE.example.sh

# Master workdir registry. Holds absolute host paths chosen by the user at
# launch time (union of env file candidates + every prior pick). Per-host
# state — regenerated by start_sandbox.sh on first run.
workdirs.txt

# Python bytecode cache. Leaks in when py_compile / pyflakes is run from
# the repo root against vertex_proxy.py.
__pycache__/

# Host-side fiss-mcp install artifacts. Only the install.sh + run-server.py
# tracked source files belong in git; the venv and cloned source tree are
# created fresh by setup_host.sh.
host_fiss_mcp/venv/
host_fiss_mcp/fiss-mcp/

# Session-history snapshots produced on demand by
# SESSION_ARCHIVE/archive_sessions.sh. The per-source subdirs hold
# hundreds of MB of session transcripts (full command + output history
# across all projects) — kept out of git for size and privacy. Only the
# script + README are tracked; re-run the script to regenerate the data.
SESSION_ARCHIVE/*/
# INDEX.md embeds first-prompt snippets from every project's sessions —
# regenerable via index_sessions.sh, kept out of git for the same
# size/privacy reasons as the archived data.
SESSION_ARCHIVE/INDEX.md
# CLASSIFIED.md embeds session titles + prompt snippets too — same
# privacy reason. It's your working attribution artifact, regenerable.
SESSION_ARCHIVE/CLASSIFIED.md

# --- fork additions (rootless podman path) ---
# uv-managed venv + pinned fiss-mcp checkout, both rebuilt by setup_host.sh.
# The venv is not relocatable (absolute paths in pyvenv.cfg and bin/ shebangs).
host_fiss_mcp/venv/
host_fiss_mcp/fiss-mcp/

# Plugin runtime state. Line 23 above states the intent -- "The plugins/cache/
# dir stays gitignored; claude-code rebuilds it from the vendored marketplaces
# tree on first session" -- but no rule ever implemented it. The `!.../plugins/`
# negation un-ignores the directory, and `claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/*`
# cannot match across a `/`, so nothing excluded the subtree and a `git add -A`
# swept 299 derived files in. These rules come last, so they win.
#
# Verified regenerable: with only plugins/marketplaces/ present, both pin
# checks pass (pin-check caveman/ponytail: OK at <sha>) and startup is clean.
#
# .in_use/<pid> are per-process lockfiles -- committing them freezes one
# container run PIDs into git, where they are stale on arrival.
claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/cache/
claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/data/
claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/installed_plugins.json
claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/known_marketplaces.json
claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/.last_inuse_sweep

# Full-resolution logo master. The committed assets/seal_sandbox.png is a
# 1200px build of it (2x the README display width, crisp on HiDPI). Keeping the
# 2816x1536 master out of git avoids ~6.7 MiB in every clone forever, which
# cannot be undone later without rewriting history.
assets/*-master.png
